EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for reaching out to Arizona State University Admission Services. Selecting the Certify this information check box at the end of the ASU admission application certifies the application is correct and complete, and the application is automatically submitted once the applicant leaves that page, even if the applicant just signs out instead of clicking the submit button.

This is why your application is submitted and you are no longer able to access the application to make corrections or pay the application fee. In order to pay your application fee now that your application has been submitted, you will need to log in to my.asu.edu to submit the application fee. You will find the application fee link under your Priority Tasks in My ASU. Click on the application fee link to enter the application fee payment page.

Please let me know if you have any further questions, or if you need assistance activating your ASURITE ID to access My ASU.

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}


If you would like any additional information or have questions related to this subject, please reply to this email.

{!Case.Thread_Id}
